Defect corrected
  Green 1.4 reported that test 2 read leaves[pin.path.join(".")] and so looked up
  "presets.0.name", while the test's own stringLeaves helper emits "presets[0].name"
  for array indices. A spec 5.4 array therefore returned undefined at that lookup.
  Green reverted its locale edit and the track blocked on the test.

Change made (smallest option, array shape kept)
  1. Added leafKey(path), which renders a traversal path as the bracket-indexed leaf
     key stringLeaves emits: numeric segments become [n], other segments use dot form.
  2. Refactored stringLeaves to accumulate path segments and emit keys through
     leafKey, so the map and the pin lookups derive from one shared renderer.
  3. Test 2 now reads leaves[leafKey(pin.path)] in en and th.
  4. Added one self-check in the en pins case: every pin path must resolve to a
     string in the en tree, with leafKey(pin.path) in the assertion message. It sits
     after the count assertion, so the Red failure stays identical and a later path
     typo fails at the pin table instead of as a copy mismatch.
  No pinned string, coverage area, test case, or assertion was removed or weakened.
  presets stays an array as spec 5.4 and 5.3 require.

Exact pin path form settled on
  Leaf-map key form: presets[0].name, presets[1].setup, presets[2].result (bracket form).
  Traversal path form inside PINS: ["presets","0","name"] and so on, because read()
  walks arrays with numeric string keys. leafKey() converts one to the other.

